+You are the fix6-fresh-data fixer for melon-seek (repo at /home/user/melon-seek, branch claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp). It is a zero-build vanilla ES-module app. You are in your own git worktree: first run `git fetch origin claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp && git checkout --detach origin/claude/stoic-ride-54ddxp` (head 6713c84 or later). Read docs/CONTRACT.md, docs/strategy/ROADMAP.md §8 (the UI simplicity budget), docs/process/PLAYBOOK.md (including "Checkpoints"), docs/process/TEMPLATE.md, and the lead log's newest sections in docs/process/lead.md.
+
+**Fix these findings for targets `/melon-seek/` and `/melon-seek/beta/`.** Five e2e checks went red on the 2026-10-16 crawl. Each also fails on the unchanged head with the same data, so the cause is new data meeting old code or old test assumptions. For each one, first decide with evidence from the data whether the PRODUCT is wrong (fix the product) or the TEST's assumption about the data no longer holds (rewrite the test so it still checks the same intent on whatever data is present, without weakening it). Never skip or delete a check.
+1. `Beta desktop QA: [D-23] the Location filter lists no bare country codes, "Republic of" or "Unknown Region" on the big-tech boards` (test/e2e/beta-desktop-qa*.e2e.js). Today: `raw location names: microsoft: "JO" (1)`. A Microsoft posting's place reads as a bare "JO" (Jordan?). Find where Microsoft's places are normalized and why "JO" isn't resolved to a country name.
+2. `Fix3 app: [BP-10] a place carries across boards by the place, not by each board's label ("Columbus, OH" -> "Columbus")`. Today: `Google's own key for Columbus, OH: expected "Columbus", got ""`. Does Google list no Columbus posting today (then the test must choose a place that both boards list from the data), or is the place key broken?
+3. `Fix3 app: [BP-14] "What they look for" shows "Required" and "Nice to have" when the posting has preferred qualifications`. Today: `no sub-headings without a preferred list: expected 0, got 2`. Find the 2 postings and decide.
+4. `fix3-data: [static beta] pay labels, tags, levels, sections, departments and places in the bundle`. Today: `google: 1 data-centre technician postings tagged TPUs/GCP/Transformers, e.g. Data Center Facilities Technician, Mechanical: TPUs,GCP,Networking,Datacenters,Mechanical design`. This is a keyword-tagging rule in server/keywords.js.
+5. `Compstimate: T20 "Same role elsewhere" -> OpenAI sets rf=swe&s=Senior; Level Senior; basis at OpenAI; Back reopens the drawer`. Today: a timeout waiting for `#drawer .ms-comps__row` with "OpenAI". Find out whether today's OpenAI data has no Senior SWE comparison row (the data changed), or whether the comparison is broken. The fix-density lane just rewrote drawer captions and text into "Details" disclosures (commits 417aa18…5f8b599, now on the branch), so also check whether the row is now inside a closed Details.
+
+**Data:** today's crawl is at /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/wt-data2/data/snapshots and .../wt-data2/data/beta/snapshots. Symlink them as data/snapshots and data/beta/snapshots in your worktree, and never commit them. Build: `node scripts/build-static.js` (writes your worktree's dist/, which is yours). Run a single e2e check with `NODE_PATH=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/pw/node_modules node scripts/e2e.js --grep='<regex>'`.
